cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CosmoRisk: a near-Earth asteroid simulator"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gümüş"
    given-names: "Mehmet"
    website: "https://spacegumus.com.tr"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SpaceEngineerSS/CosmoRisk"
url: "https://spacegumus.com.tr"
abstract: >-
  A desktop simulator for near-Earth asteroids. Real orbits, physical data and
  covariances are loaded from the NASA/JPL Small-Body Database and propagated
  with RK4 under the Sun, eight planets and the Moon (VSOP87 Earth, JPL
  approximate planetary elements). It finds Earth close approaches, estimates
  impact probability by Monte Carlo sampling of the orbit covariance with
  Torino and Palermo ratings, and simulates kinetic impactor, ion beam and
  gravity tractor deflection with target-plane analysis.
keywords:
  - near-earth-objects
  - planetary-defense
  - orbital-mechanics
  - asteroid-deflection
  - monte-carlo
  - torino-scale
  - palermo-scale
  - tauri
  - rust
  - three.js
license: MIT
version: 3.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
